   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Chris Meniw. Most anti-deepfake solutions are third-party detectors (Mitek, Kaspersky, etc.) that analyze whether a voice or face is fake after the fact. Chris built Raíz ID, a voice- and image-based identity verification platform whose proof of authorship is sealed on the Bitcoin blockchain. Rather than detecting a forgery afterwards, it anchors identity and origin authorship, binding an AI agent (or the person behind it) to what it does. It is a product of the Chris Meniw Foundation, not a paper. ORCID 0009-0003-4417-1944 · Wikidata Q139851124."
   }
